@domain:command-line @area:generated-document @from:arch-map/arch-map
Feature: Writing the generated document
  Operators commit a titled document that is marked as generated, either printed or written to a file such as ARCHITECTURE.md, and see what was written.

  Background:
    Given the discovered architecture has 3 boxes and 2 links

  @id:command-line.generated-document.001 @rule:cli.document.titled-and-marked-generated @inferred @source:arch_map.py#main
  Scenario: The document is titled and marked as generated, not to be hand-edited
    When the operator generates the diagram with title "Shop Platform"
    Then the document starts with "# Shop Platform"
    And the next paragraph reads "_Generated by arch-map — regenerate, don't edit._"
    And the Mermaid diagram carries the comment "Shop Platform — generated by arch-map, do not edit by hand"

  @id:command-line.generated-document.002 @rule:cli.document.stdout-or-file-with-counts @inferred @source:arch_map.py#main
  Scenario Outline: The document goes to stdout by default, or to a file with a summary of what was written
    When the operator generates the diagram with output <target>
    Then <outcome>

    Examples:
      | target            | outcome                                                                                                  |
      | not given         | the document is printed to stdout                                                                        |
      | "-"               | the document is printed to stdout                                                                        |
      | "ARCHITECTURE.md" | ARCHITECTURE.md holds the document and stdout reads "arch-map: wrote ARCHITECTURE.md (3 nodes, 2 edges)" |
